<p>UK facilities management is under constant pressure to deliver more for less. Tight SLAs, rising energy costs, complex compliance landscapes, and client demands for measurable sustainability improvements make efficient operations critical. AI is helping FM providers shift from reactive firefighting to predictive, optimised service delivery.</p>
<p>Generic AI tools don't understand facilities management. They can't tell the difference between a critical BMS alarm and a routine maintenance request. They don't understand your SLA commitments or the contractual penalties for missed response times. Generic scheduling tools don't account for engineer skills, qualifications, and geographical constraints. They create schedules that look efficient on paper but fail in the real world.</p>
<p>Bespoke AI solutions are built around your contracts, your buildings, and your engineers. We train predictive maintenance models on your BMS data and your maintenance history, calibrated to the specific equipment types in your portfolio. We build job prioritisation that reflects your SLA commitments and the risk profile of each site. We create engineer scheduling that accounts for qualifications, traffic patterns, parts availability, and first-time fix probability, not just distance.</p>
<p>Compliance in FM is complex and high-stakes. Missing a gas safety inspection or a fire system test isn't just a contractual failure; it's a safety risk and a legal liability. AI can monitor every compliance requirement across every site in your portfolio, flagging approaching deadlines and generating evidence of compliance automatically. We ensure all data processing meets UK GDPR requirements, particularly for building access and occupancy data, and that AI-assisted compliance records meet the evidential standards auditors and clients expect.</p>
<p>We worked with a UK FM provider managing 200+ commercial buildings under hard FM contracts. Reactive callouts were consuming 60% of the maintenance budget, and compliance tracking was managed across spreadsheets with frequent near-misses. Our predictive maintenance model, integrated with BMS data across 80 monitored sites, reduced reactive callouts by 35% in six months. The AI compliance monitoring system eliminated missed certificate renewals entirely and reduced audit preparation time from two weeks to two days. Energy optimisation across the monitored portfolio delivered an 18% reduction in HVAC energy consumption.</p>

